    "negative_control": {
      "column": "nc_prior_chloride",
      "margin": 0.5,
      "definition": "last chemistry chloride sampled 24-48 h before time zero; disjoint from the baseline window (24 h before time zero), so never the same specimen as baseline_chloride; cannot be caused by the assignment; analysed complete-case in stays that have it (having the earlier sample is pre-treatment), weighted by a propensity model refitted in that subset",
      "rationale": "falsification test for confounding that also acts on earlier chloride (e.g. clinicians choosing lactated Ringer's for a rising chloride or acidosis that the last baseline value does not capture); a pass does not bound confounding of the primary outcome; margin 0.5 mmol/L is investigator-chosen"
    },
    "benchmark_direction": "negative",
    "benchmark_note": "investigator-chosen directional compatibility check: primary 95% CI entirely below -0.5 mmol/L (balanced fluids lower chloride in SMART, BaSICS and PLUS under sustained fluid policies; those trials do not supply a numerical range for this initiation contrast); not RCT effect reproduction and not validation of identification",
